        "behållare",
        "container"
      ],
      "dcDescription": [
        "The water container's main body is made by copper with brass and silver plate ornaments. It is inserted in a wooden container. It is used to carry water to monasteries, or monastery retreats, that are situated on hilltops, or other places difficult to reach. It has been carried on the back.\nThe container was brought from the Yarlung area, and had belonged to a monastery there. The container was made in the 17th century or earlier.\nThe lower part of the carrying frame has more recently been replaced./HWq 1997.12.0003 The object was 'almost black' when it arrived to the middlemen, i.e. the silve"
      ],
